## Summary

I ported the web `EntryDrawer` (DLQ-inspector entry drawer) to a production-quality, native Apple/SwiftUI surface at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/EntryDrawer.*`, following the established `AuditPanel`/`EntriesTable` conventions for the same web feature.

**Delivered (10 files, ~2,300 lines):**
- `EntryDrawer.Models.swift` — `DLQDrawerSummary`/`DLQDrawerFull` snake-case decode, `decodeBase64Utf8` payload codec (fatal-UTF8 parity), ISO-8601/number formatting
- `EntryDrawer.Projection.swift` — head/payload projection + the exhaustive presentation resolver (loading/content/empty/error/offline/stale) and the `replayDisabled` rule
- `EntryDrawer.Model.swift` — `@Observable` model + P1/S8 `EntryDrawerFullSource` seam (no HTTP in the view)
- `EntryDrawer.Strings.swift` / `.strings` — P1/S10 i18n facade with every extracted web key + native chrome
- `EntryDrawer.Components.swift` / `EntryDrawer.swift` — detail KV panel, inner/raw payload viewer (tabs + copy + `<pre>`), footer Replay/Close CTAs, freshness chip, state views, and a `.entryDrawer(isPresented:)` sheet presenter with dismiss semantics; emits P1/S11 `view.opened`
- `EntryDrawer.Previews.swift` + `EntryDrawer.Tests.swift`/`.ModelTests.swift` — per-state previews + 25 unit tests

**Faithful parity fix:** matched the web's exact `loading && !full → Spinner` branch (head hidden during load; title still shows the summary id) — caught and corrected during testing, along with a real bug where `%lld` locale-grouping wrongly rendered "DLQ entry #8,841".

**Verification (Xcode 26.5 via `DEVELOPER_DIR`):**
- swiftformat `--lint` 0/9 · swiftlint `--strict` **0 violations/9 files** · placeholder gate **0**
- Isolated SwiftPM build (Swift 6 strict concurrency) + **25/25 XCTest pass**
- `swiftc -typecheck` clean on **iOS 18 simulator + macOS 15** SDKs
- `xcodegen generate` enumerates all 10 files

The full-app `xcodebuild build test` (iOS+macOS) is **macOS-pending**, blocked solely by **pre-existing baseline** issues (170 feature-views `*.Tests.swift` importing XCTest into the app target; macOS dev-signing) — **0 `EntryDrawer` errors** — and is deferred to the P99 acceptance gate per `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md`/ADR-012, exactly as prior P4 surfaces. The log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`, with the full-app deferral disclosed honestly. Committed only the allowed files (shared `project.yml`/`.swiftlint.yml` were temporarily registered for verification, then reverted, so the build wiring stays owned by P4-core integration).

